From: PyDevices usbif
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shared/tinyusb: let a user C module extend the built-in
 configuration descriptor

Purpose: usbif's isochronous classes (UAC, later UVC) must be *built-in*
interfaces rather than runtime ones. TinyUSB dispatches each interface to
application drivers before built-in ones, and MicroPython's runtime driver
(runtime_dev_open) claims every interface numbered at or above
USBD_ITF_BUILTIN_MAX whatever its class -- so an audio interface declared from
Python is claimed by Python, and TinyUSB's audiod_open() is never called.
Python cannot service isochronous endpoints, which is the whole reason usbif
exists in C.

This is the descriptor half of the extension hook added by patch 0001: a length
contribution and a descriptor block, both supplied by a module-owned header, so
no volatile content lands in MicroPython.

Provenance: written for usbif Phase 1, 2026-08-29, after reading usbd.c's
driver dispatch order (_app_driver is consulted before _usbd_driver) and
mp_usbd_runtime.c's open callback.
Upstream-version range: authored against v1.28.0.
Order: applies after 0001.
Test: build a board whose MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_TUSB_CONFIG header enables
CFG_TUD_AUDIO and defines MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_DESC_CFG; the board must enumerate
as a composite CDC + audio function and keep its REPL.

--- a/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd.h
+++ b/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd.h
@@ -89,10 +89,16 @@
 // length (2 * bytes_len + 1) (including NUL terminator).
 void mp_usbd_hex_str(char *out_str, const uint8_t *bytes, size_t bytes_len);
 
-// Length of built-in configuration descriptor
+// Length of built-in configuration descriptor.
+// A user C module may contribute further built-in interfaces; the header named
+// by MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_TUSB_CONFIG (see tusb_config.h) defines their length.
+#ifndef MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_DESC_CFG_LEN
+#define MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_DESC_CFG_LEN (0)
+#endif
 #define MP_USBD_BUILTIN_DESC_CFG_LEN (TUD_CONFIG_DESC_LEN +                     \
     (CFG_TUD_CDC ? (TUD_CDC_DESC_LEN) : 0) +  \
-    (CFG_TUD_MSC ? (TUD_MSC_DESC_LEN) : 0)    \
+    (CFG_TUD_MSC ? (TUD_MSC_DESC_LEN) : 0) +  \
+    MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_DESC_CFG_LEN           \
     )
 
 // Built-in USB device and configuration descriptor values
--- a/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_descriptor.c
+++ b/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_descriptor.c
@@ -64,6 +64,9 @@
     #if CFG_TUD_MSC
     TUD_MSC_DESCRIPTOR(USBD_ITF_MSC, USBD_STR_MSC, EPNUM_MSC_OUT, EPNUM_MSC_IN, USBD_MSC_IN_OUT_MAX_SIZE),
     #endif
+    #ifdef MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_DESC_CFG
+    MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_DESC_CFG
+    #endif
 };
 
 const uint16_t *tud_descriptor_string_cb(uint8_t index, uint16_t langid) {
